Crow v1.2.1.2: bounded request bodies (phto plan: loose-ends L1).

Stock Crow appends the whole request body to request::body before any middleware or
handler runs, so the application cannot refuse or stream a large upload. This patch adds
two generic, opt-in hooks; with neither used, behaviour is unchanged:

  * App::header_filter(f): called when the request headers are complete, before the body
    is read (and before "100 Continue"). f may set request::body_sink / request::user_data.
    Returning false rejects the request: the response f filled in is sent, the connection
    is closed and a bounded amount of the remaining input is swallowed (so the client can
    read the response instead of seeing a reset).
  * request::body_sink(chunk, len, res): when set, receives each body chunk instead of
    request::body. Returning false rejects the request the same way.

All policy (limits, spooling to disk) lives in the application, not here.

